   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 491 of the laws of 2018 relating to incorporating the\nVolunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent Association of Whitehall, New York\nand providing for its powers and duties, in relation to the disposition of\nforeign fire insurance premium taxes received by such corporation",
    "basePrintNo": "S4160",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4160-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7, Chap 491 of 2018",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4160           REVISED MEMO 03/04/2019\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 491 of the laws of 2018 relat-\ning to incorporating the Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent Asso-\nciation of Whitehall, New York and providing for its powers and duties,\nin relation to the disposition of foreign fire insurance premium taxes\nreceived by such corporation\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation relates to the disposition of foreign fire insurance\npremium taxes received by the Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent\nAssociation of Whitehall, New York.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one establishes the precept for the Volunteer Exempt Firefight-\ner's Benevolent Association of Whitehall to collect foreign fire insur-\nance premium taxes. The officer of the Volunteer Exempt Firefighter\nBenevolent Association of Whitehall will assume all powers and be\nsubject to all provisions pertaining to treasurers of fire departments.\n\nSection two sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn prior similar bills, from consultation with the New York State Comp-\ntroller's office, it is necessary to amend chapter 491 of the laws of\n2018 to take out language that limits the use of the foreign fire insur-\nance premium taxes received by the Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benev-\nolent Association of Whitehall, New York.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
